-- Live-only spell_dbc / talent_dbc / talenttab_dbc state that no SQL file on disk writes: what early generate.py runs
-- (2026-08-24..10-12) applied live from pending migrations that were deleted before commit (the live `updates` table
-- still lists 285 such PENDING files). Dumped from the live DB on 2026-11-05 (`replay_diff.py --whole` live-only
-- rows and index cells). Sibling of live_secondary_rows.sql, which holds the 300xx duration/range/radius rows these
-- spells point at.
--
-- What it holds:
--   - spell_dbc 2,273 rows, all stock ids: the client DBC's values except the Duration/Range/EffectRadius indices,
--     which point at the value-equal 300xx secondary rows (and a few locale strings); talent_dbc 220 rows equal to
--     the client DBC; talenttab_dbc 30 rows (BackgroundFile holds a number where the DBC has a texture name).
--   - Guarded remaps: 4,926 index cells of rows a file on disk writes with a stock index while live points at the
--     value-equal 300xx row (spell 48815's CastingTimeIndex 30017 is the one remap whose value differs).
--
-- Statement shapes keep it safe to replay after every file: `INSERT IGNORE` never overrides a row a file wrote, and
-- each UPDATE only changes a cell that still holds the value the remap replaced. No id is in a reserved block
-- (ids.yaml: spell 200000-209999, talent 60000-60799, talenttab 60800-60999).
--
-- Read by the whole-table check (lib/replay_diff.py) only, not by state.load_existing_rows: generate.py's state
-- already holds every one of these ids from the client DBC, and with the remaps in its state a full run re-emits
-- ~3,800 stock spells and the 200000-209999 block pointing back at the stock indices (tested 2026-11-05).
-- Never edit a row here to change a spell; declare it in source/ and let generate.py emit it.

-- spell_dbc: 2273 live-only rows.

-- spell_dbc: 4926 live-only secondary-row remaps on rows a file on disk writes, guarded by the value they replace.
